All six features implemented in two files, `app/auth.py` and `app/main.py`. Models and database untouched.

**`app/auth.py`** — `require_api_key` reads `X-API-Key` via `Header`, raises `HTTPException(401)` for a missing or unknown key, and returns the username (`VALID_API_KEYS` value) on success.

**`app/main.py`** — the full CRUD surface:
- `GET /tasks` now takes `status` (typed as `TaskStatus`, so FastAPI validates it), `priority`, `assigned_to`, plus `page` (default 1) and `page_size` (default 20). Filters are applied in sequence and combined; pagination slices after filtering.
- `POST /tasks` — `Depends(require_api_key)`, 404 if `project_id` isn't in `projects`, next ID is `max(existing ids) + 1`, returns 201 with the created task.
- `PUT /tasks/{task_id}` — auth, 404 if missing, applies only the fields present in the body via `model_dump(exclude_unset=True)`.
- `DELETE /tasks/{task_id}` — auth, 404 if missing, 204 on success.

